{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pbpxL8vNTS9jdqTBa3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both items in ticket 13 are done, in three commits. The external player watcher and the VLC probe can no longer leave a child process behind.\n\n1. **VLC probe deadline** (`68caed9`). The old `answers_version` called `.status()`, which blocks with no time limit. It now hands off to `answers_version_within(candidate, PROBE_TIMEOUT)` with a 5-second limit. That function starts the probe and checks on it every 25 ms (the existing `POLL` interval). If the candidate is still running at the deadline, or `try_wait` errors, it goes through the existing `end()`, which kills and reaps it, and the candidate counts as \"not answering\". There are two new tests in `src-tauri/src/external_player.rs`:\n   - A Node script that never exits is reported as not answering, the probe returns soon after its deadline, and the script's process is no longer running afterwards.\n   - A candidate that exits cleanly in time still counts as VLC.\n\n   The first test started out failing because the function didn't exist yet.\n2. **`try_wait` error in `watch`** (`a4c134b`). That path used to drop the child, which in Rust neither kills nor reaps it. It now takes the child out of its slot and passes it to `end()`. As the ticket says, there's no automated test for this, because the OS error can't be triggered on demand, so I skipped writing a test first and wrote that down in the notes.\n3. **`src-tauri/AGENTS.md`** (`41a3f11`). I added a rule to the external player section: every child this module starts must end through `end()`, and probes must never use `.status()` or `.output()`.\n\n**Checks:** `npm test` passes (lint, depcheck and 4224 unit tests). Since `npm test` doesn't run the Rust tests, I also ran the full `cargo test` (211 passed), `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`, all clean.\n\n`cargo test` won't compile until `build-tauri/` exists, so I ran `npm run build:tauri` first. I put that, and the fact that the crate has no library target (use `cargo test external_player`, not `--lib`), in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":66550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb328e1e-7d30-4abb-b61c-f9c4b744f300","uuid":"c0dbbf34-76f9-4a2f-bfb4-6e98070b65f1","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:18:23.211Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pbpdyaNeSZdmY7591b"}
